      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: session menu adds Open PR, Open in editor, and numbered group shortcuts",
        "body": "Closes #104153\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWork sessions (sessions bound to a managed worktree) already detect their pull request (chat PR chips) and have a local checkout, but the session context menu offers no way to reach either: jumping to a session's PR or opening its worktree in an editor means opening the chat first or digging through the Worktrees page. The Move to group submenu is also mouse-only, while every other menu item has a single-letter shortcut.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe session list (app sidebar and Sessions page) is where session triage happens, so the per-session context menu is the natural home for these jump actions. All the data already exists behind gateway methods (`controlUi.sessionPullRequests`, `worktrees.list`) and the editor URL schemes already power the chat file sidebar's \"Open in editor\" button, so the menu only needed the surface, not new backend capability.\n\n## User Impact\n\nFor sessions bound to a worktree, the session context menu now shows:\n\n- **Open PR** (shortcut `G`) — opens the pull request detected on the session's branch (active PRs preferred over merged/closed). Rendered disabled until the lazy lookup resolves so the menu never shifts under the pointer; stays disabled when no PR exists.\n- **Open in** submenu — opens the worktree checkout in Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, or Zed via their URL schemes (same mechanism as the chat file sidebar).\n\nFor every session, the **Move to group** submenu entries are now numbered (1-9): existing groups first, then Remove from group, then New group…, matching the order users scan. Pressing a digit files the session immediately. Plain chat sessions see no new items.\n\n| Menu (light) | Move to group | Open in |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![Session menu with Open PR and Open in](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/menu-light.png) | ![Numbered group submenu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/move-to-group-light.png) | ![Editor submenu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/open-in-light.png) |\n\nDark mode: [menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/menu-dark.png) · [groups](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/move-to-group-dark.png) · [editors](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-menu-work-actions/open-in-dark.png)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Menu surface polish (follow-up commit `f7ae085b389`): the menu now promotes itself to the browser popover top layer — sidebar-hosted menus render inside the nav stacking context (z-index 10) which paints below the sidebar resizer divider (z-index 20), so the divider line used to bleed through the menu. Same pattern as `openclaw-native-link-menu`. The four menu surfaces sharing the hardcoded `0 18px 40px` drop shadow now use the theme token `var(--shadow-lg)` (much softer in light mode). Screenshots above are regenerated with these fixes.\n- Screenshots above were captured against the deterministic mock-gateway harness (`ui/src/test-helpers/control-ui-e2e.ts`) with a worktree session, a detected open PR, and four groups.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/components/session-menu.test.ts ui/src/components/session-menu-work.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-sidebar.test.ts` — 32 tests passed (new coverage: numbered digit shortcuts and ordering, Open PR loading/enabled dispatch, editor submenu dispatch, PR-pick preference, worktree path resolution incl. removed worktrees).\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/sessions/sessions-page.test.ts ui/src/pages/sessions/view.test.ts ui/src/components/app-sidebar.test.ts` — 54 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.ui.json` clean; oxlint/oxfmt clean on touched files.\n- i18n: `control-ui-i18n.ts sync --write` translated the two new strings across all 20 locales with `fallbacks=0`.\n\nImplementation notes for reviewers:\n\n- `editorOpenUrl` moved from `ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-sidebar.ts` to `ui/src/lib/editor-links.ts` (shared by the chat file sidebar and both menu hosts); the old export is deleted.\n- The PR/worktree lookup is lazy and versioned: hosts fetch on menu open via `ui/src/components/session-menu-work.ts` and drop stale responses when the menu closes or switches sessions. The menu items carry their payload in the action, so no host state is read after close.\n- `activateMenuShortcut` now accepts digits; digit targets only exist in the DOM while a submenu is open, so closed menus ignore them.\n\n",
